  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1220 PM CST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nA surface low in the northeastern Gulf that has created our \npersistent northeasterly flow will finally begin to move away from \nthe area Saturday. This will allow our winds to turn to the \nsoutheast, bringing more moisture into South Texas. A cold front \nwill move through the area Sunday, bringing with it a low to medium \n(30-70%) chances of showers. Cloud cover will linger behind the \nfront until another reinforcing surge of high pressure moves through \nsometime Tuesday, bringing in drier air.\n\nMinor coastal flooding will remain a threat through the weekend as \nhigher than normal tides and long period swells continue.",
